# SRG-APP-000172-AU-002550  -  CAT I
# For accounts using password authentication, the Central Log Server must
# use FIPS-validated SHA-1 or later protocol to protect the integrity of the
# password authentication process.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000172-AU-002550
group:           V-206475
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-000197
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk can be started in FIPS mode so that the whole instance uses
                 FIPS-validated algorithms, and the hash applied to stored passwords is
                 selected by passwordHashAlgorithm, which together cover the product's part
                 of protecting the integrity of the password authentication process.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.
governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
check:           authentication.conf [authentication] passwordHashAlgorithm matches ^SHA(256|512)-crypt(-[1-9][0-9]{3,})?$
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          authentication.conf [authentication] passwordHashAlgorithm https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic module shipped with the platform,
                 and the host kernel's FIPS state
external:        FIPS mode is an install-time decision (splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-130):
                 turning it on after first start requires a reinstall or upgrade, which is
                 a deployment action rather than a configuration change
external:        Password verification for accounts held in LDAP or SAML is performed by
                 that provider's cryptographic module
external:        Re-hashing of passwords stored before the algorithm was set, which this
                 setting does not perform: an existing hash keeps the algorithm it was
                 written with until the password is next changed.

citation:        SPLK-CL-000390 check text ("splunk show fips-mode" must return FIPS mode
                 enabled) and fix text (SPLUNK_COMMON_CRITERIA=1 and SPLUNK_FIPS=1 in
                 splunk-launch.conf before first start); splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-130
                 (SPLUNK_FIPS vocabulary [0|1], one-time setting, cannot be reversed
                 without reinstall); authentication.conf.spec:58-80
finding:         splunk-launch.conf does not set SPLUNK_FIPS = 1, or authentication.conf
                 passwordHashAlgorithm is outside the SHA256-crypt and SHA512-crypt
                 families, so the application does not protect the password authentication
                 process with a FIPS-validated hash.
